{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"The ledger now has 64 metric entries read from five lab result files, with result and job hashes. D036 has no lab `result.json`; I’ve recorded its binary-swap text hash as corroborating evidence and left paired-PPL inheritance dependent on D029. The tests cover rules a–d and unknown combinations; I’m updating the superseded planner expectations and documenting the 32k memory limit."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='cc/moe_planner/test_quality_ledger.py';s=open(p).read().replace('1315.258','1316.605');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='cc/moe_planner/PLANNER.md';s=open(p).read().replace('artifacts/codexPL2/', 'artifacts/codexPL3/')\ns=s.replace('cc/moe_planner/test_plan.py --basetemp=', 'cc/moe_planner --basetemp=')\ns=s.replace('\"'`--budget-host-mib`, `--max-kld`,'\"', '\"'`--budget-host-mib`, `--max-kld`, `--quality-ledger`,'\"')\ns=s.replace('\"'`max_quality_loss` (mean KLD), and `objective`.'\"', '\"'`max_quality_loss` (mean KLD), `max_ppl_change` (API only; default 0.01), and `objective`. KLD and relative PPL change are separate metrics and are never added or numerically equated.'\"')\ns=s.replace('q8_reuse preserves computation in its measured regime; it does not\\\\nmake representation, placement or quantized-KV KLD known.', 'q8_reuse inherits an established base quality only through rule a below; its speed transfer remains extrapolated.')\na=s.index('quality risk is measured combined\\\\nKLD;');b=s.index('\\\\nThe emitted JSON',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''quality risk is measured or evidence-inherited screening KLD. Unknown/failing risk is\nJSON null and treated as +infinity for dominance, never zero. Tied\nnondominated points remain available, and the full Pareto set is not truncated\nby \"'`--top`.\n\n### Quality ledger and inheritance (T-PL3)\n\nRebuild the bundled ledger with `nice -n 10 python3 -B\ncc/moe_planner/build_quality_ledger.py`. The script reads **real**\n`lab/jobs/JOB/att-1/result.json` metrics and frozen job test definitions,\nrequiring completed, clean results. D013 predates frozen definitions, so its\nread-only `lab/tests/mem2.json` definitions and their SHA256 are recorded too.\nNo metric value is copied from decision prose. Each metric entry contains\nrepresentation, placement family/parameters, KV type, FA, enabled runtime\ncomponents, context, chunk count, metric/value, job/attempt/test, decision,\nresult path/SHA256 and job envelope SHA256. Counts:\n\n| Decision | Job | Metric entries |\n| --- | --- | ---: |\n| D013 | job-aa57700ee5 | 15 |\n| D034 | job-56115e2bf1 | 15 |\n| D035 | job-3d2fbbd061 | 27 |\n| D033 | job-a945fa8656 | 3 |\n| D029 | job-34c09bec98 | 4 |\n\nD035 PAP and imatrix measurements are recorded without activating nonexistent\nmodel variants or supplying missing timing/placement calibration. BF16 has no\nsynthetic zero entry: absent ledger evidence remains unknown. `load_quality_ledger()`\nloads the bundled JSON or `--quality-ledger PATH`; an explicit empty ledger\ncannot fall back to `calibration.json` quality priors.\n\nThe rules are scoped to matched Granite representations and static placement;\nLRU, hybrid, mismatched model bytes/layouts, new KV types, unproven components,\nand representation transfers without supporting evidence remain unknown.\nDirectly recorded representation/placement KLD is `measured` screening quality.\nOther admissible configurations are `inherited (rule x; evidence y)`:\n\n* **Rule a — computation-preserving components.**\n  [D029](../../decisions/D029-c1-q8reuse-accepted.md), job-34c09bec98,\n  provides paired OFF/ON **complete stdout SHA256 identity and exact PPL\n  identity**, independently for Q8_0 and mixE4K. The builder verifies those\n  equalities from result.json and records paired test names. Only those\n  representation/component pairs can inherit base quality; text identity\n  alone or PPL identity alone is insufficient. This is an explicit screening\n  transfer across placements/contexts, not new combined-KLD measurement.\n  [D036](../../decisions/D036-binary-component-swap.md) corroborates the Q8_0\n  binary swap using `artifacts/x7-comp/swap-gen.out` SHA256, which the builder\n  compares to D029. That manual run has **no lab job/result.json or paired PPL**;\n  it supplies no independent inheritance permission and no fabricated job ID.\n* **Rule b — static placement-only changes.**\n  [D034](../../decisions/D034-planner-validated.md), job-56115e2bf1,\n  measures mixE4K at K=19,20,21,22,23, each KLD **0.040017**, agreeing with\n  [D013](../../decisions/D013-mixed-precision-frontier.md) and D035'\"'s all-GPU\n  control. A representation must have at least two distinct measured static\n  placements with identical KLD across the available base evidence before\n  another integer \"'`--n-cpu-moe K` in [0,24] inherits it. Changing weights,\n  hybrid arithmetic or LRU is outside this rule. Other representations do\n  not inherit mixE4K'\"'s placement evidence.\n* **Rule c — KV quality and scheduler fix.**\n  [D033](../../decisions/D033-kv-quant-fixed-and-measured.md), job-a945fa8656,\n  measures paired FA-on PPL at ctx4096, six chunks: f16 **7.5385**, q8_0\n  **7.5392**, q4_0 **8.1368**. Compute relative PPL change from those ledger\n  values. q8_0 inherits mixE4K base screening KLD when within the default\n  **±1% relative PPL budget** and \"'`kv_quant_fix` is enabled. This is a policy\n  inference, not a measurement or mathematical bound on combined KLD.\n  q4_0 is `quality-failing` under that PPL budget; it never acquires a KLD\n  value even if a caller loosens the PPL budget. Unknown KV/representation\n  pairs remain unknown. The scheduler capacity correction is covered by\n  D033'\"'s f16 control and quantized variants; no general permission for other\n  engine fixes is inferred. The planner's 0.08 KLD ceiling does not mean an\n  8% PPL budget.\n* **Rule d — FA evidence caveat.**\n  D033's paired PPL has FA on only. Emit **“PPL measured with FA only; no\n  non-FA PPL comparison”** as a caveat, not a block, for supported FA\n  combinations. Do not claim measured FA equivalence or transfer this\n  exception to representations without D033 evidence.\n\n\"'`quality` includes status, description, rule IDs, decision/job/test evidence,\nPPL relative change/status, and caveats. `kld` and Pareto `quality_risk` contain\nthe inherited base value only after all applicable rules succeed. A finite\n`--max-kld` rejects unknown, failing, or above-ceiling values, regardless of\n`--allow-extrapolation`. With no ceiling, unknown/failing candidates can be\nreturned as exploratory hypotheses, visibly labeled and retaining null risk.\nThe quality caveats preserve measurement scope: KLD is 20x512 wikitext vs\nBF16 logits, PPL is six chunks at ctx4096; neither certifies long-context or\ngeneral-task quality. GPU/decode confidence remains independent of quality.\n'\"''' +s[b:]\na=s.index('With extrapolation enabled, the 900 MiB top five');s=s[:a]+'''With the accepted factory runtime components (\"'`q8_reuse`, `kv_quant_fix`),\n900 MiB / ctx4096 / max-KLD 0.08 returns mixE4K static19, f16 KV,\n875.867 MiB GPU + 2 MiB guard, 152.625 predicted decode t/s, KLD 0.040017\ninherited through rules a/c (D029/D033), with direct placement evidence D034.\nNo extrapolation flag is needed for its baseline GPU/decode regime.\n\nThe required **1200 MiB / ctx32768 / max-KLD 0.08** rerun returns **no feasible\nplan** under the existing memory model. This is a memory constraint after the\nquality repair: the smallest quality-admissible candidate is mixE4K static24,\nq8_0 KV, FA on, batch512/ubatch128, **1314.605 MiB GPU + 2 MiB guard =\n1316.605 MiB**. The D028 FA anchor is ~2762 MiB all-GPU/f16 at 32k;\nq8 KV saves 720 MiB, all 24 expert layers on CPU save the fitted placement\namount, and ubatch128 saves 81 MiB. The result is still above 1200 MiB.\nChanging quality rules cannot remove those bytes. The earlier q4_0 example\nwas rejected by D033 and is withdrawn. No smaller memory prediction or new\nunmeasured placement is invented to satisfy this scenario.\n\nAt **1317 MiB** the same ctx32768 / max-KLD 0.08 request has a feasible q8_0\ncandidate with inherited quality (rules a/b/c/d; D029/D034/D033). Its memory,\ndecode and prefill remain extrapolated; the quality value is a screening prior.\n`artifacts/codexPL3/` contains the exact commands, both requested reruns,\na 1317 MiB diagnostic rerun, ledger counts, emitted lab definitions, and CPU-only\npytest output. No Docker/GPU operation was performed. Long-context quality,\nactual TTFT/host working set and post-fix combined performance still need\nmeasurement.\n'\"'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 nice -n 10 python3 -m pytest cc/moe_planner -q -p no:cacheprovider --basetemp=artifacts/codexPL3/pytest-tmp > artifacts/codexPL3/pytest.txt 2>&1; cat artifacts/codexPL3/pytest.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
